
== G1 effect names a ?variable its condition never binds
   Rule r1 when at(ann, hall) { Assert marked(?t). }
   ACCEPTED by ModuleCompiler.validate
   fact + marked(?t)

== G2 effect names a ?variable bound only under not
   Rule r2 when not marked(?t) { Assert lit(?t). }
   ACCEPTED by ModuleCompiler.validate
   fact + lit(?t)

== G3 ?variable bound to a group written where a thing is expected
   Rule r3 when at(?g, hall) { Assert marked(?g). Increase count(?g) by 1. }
   ACCEPTED by ModuleCompiler.validate
   fact + count(ann) = 1
   fact + count(bob) = 1
   fact + marked(ann)
   fact + marked(bob)

== G4 compared ?variable bound only on the other side of an or (bound() treats or as and)
   Entity cellar: place "the cellar".
   Rule r4 when at(?g, cellar) or gold(?g) > 5 says "{?g} is rich or below." { Assert lit(cup). }
   ACCEPTED by ModuleCompiler.validate

== G5 compared ?variable hidden in arithmetic escapes bound()
   Rule r5 when gold(?g) + 0 > 5 { Assert lit(cup). }
   ACCEPTED by ModuleCompiler.validate

== G5b same comparison without arithmetic (control)
   Rule r5b when gold(?g) > 5 { Assert lit(cup). }
   REJECTED: Rule r5b compares ?g, which nothing in its condition binds

== G6 measure interpolation with a ?variable in a rule says renders the unbound measure
   Rule r6 when at(?g, hall) and gold(?g) > 5 says "{?g} counts {gold(?g)} coins." { Assert lit(cup). }
   ACCEPTED by ModuleCompiler.validate
   fact + lit(cup)
   said r6: Ann counts 0 coins.

== G7 measure interpolation with a ?variable the condition never binds
   Rule r7 when at(ann, hall) says "Someone counts {gold(?nobody)} coins." { Assert lit(cup). }
   ACCEPTED by ModuleCompiler.validate
   fact + lit(cup)
   said r7: Someone counts 0 coins.

== G8 ending epilogue naming what its condition bound: told right as it happens, raw on the closing page
   Ending won "Won" when at(?g, hall) and gold(?g) > 5 "{?g} leaves rich.".
   ACCEPTED by ModuleCompiler.validate
   fact + concluded()
   fact + reached(won)
   said won: Ann leaves rich.
   closing page (Endings.reached): {"title":"Won","lines":["?g leaves rich."]}

== G9 query body comparing a ?variable nothing binds: always false, accepted
   Query rich() means gold(?g) > 5.
   Rule r9 when rich() { Assert lit(cup). }
   ACCEPTED by ModuleCompiler.validate

== G10 distinct over an unbound ?variable: accepted, throws when the world runs
   Rule r10 when at(ann, ?p) and distinct(ann, ?other) { Assert lit(cup). }
   ACCEPTED by ModuleCompiler.validate
   RUNTIME THROW: distinct compares two bound parties

== G11 Observation text naming a ?variable its condition never binds (Rule says checks this; Observe does not)
   Observe o1 at hall when at(ann, hall) "{?who} waits here.".
   ACCEPTED by ModuleCompiler.validate
   observation renders: ?who waits here.

== G13 Rule writing a Query name (control)
   Query rich(g: group) means gold(g) > 5.
   Rule r13 when at(ann, hall) { Assert rich(ann). }
   REJECTED: Unknown function or arity: rich(ann)

== G14 authored relation colliding with an Event latch
   Relation once_e().
   Event e when at(ann, hall) "It happens.".
   REJECTED: Duplicate function once_e

== G15 authored relation colliding with Endings' concluded (silently merged: the author's fact ends the book)
   Relation concluded().
   Ending fin "Fin" when lit(cup) "The end.".
   Rule r15 when at(ann, hall) and not concluded() { Assert concluded(). }
   Rule r15b when at(ann, hall) { Assert lit(cup). }
   ACCEPTED by ModuleCompiler.validate
   fact + concluded()
   fact + lit(cup)

== G16 literal braces in authored text
   Rule r16 when at(ann, hall) says "A sign: {no entry}." { Assert lit(cup). }
   REJECTED: Invalid predicate: Line 1, col 4:
